{"audio": "romans-10.opus", "duration_ms": 165006, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 2080, "end_ms": 3380, "text": "Romans, Chapter Ten."}, {"start_ms": 4840, "end_ms": 10200, "text": "Brothers, my heart’s desire and prayer to God for the Israelites is for their salvation."}, {"start_ms": 10780, "end_ms": 16081, "text": "For I testify about them that they are zealous for God, but not on the basis of knowledge."}, {"start_ms": 16741, "end_ms": 23861, "text": "Because they were ignorant of God’s righteousness and sought to establish their own, they did not submit to God’s righteousness."}, {"start_ms": 24421, "end_ms": 28941, "text": "For Christ is the end of the law, to bring righteousness to everyone who believes."}, {"start_ms": 29341, "end_ms": 43122, "text": "For concerning the righteousness that is by the law, Moses writes: “The man who does these things will live by them.” But the righteousness that is by faith says: “Do not say in your heart, ‘Who will ascend into heaven?’ (that is,"}, {"start_ms": 43202, "end_ms": 51122, "text": "to bring Christ down) or, ‘Who will descend into the Abyss?’ (that is, to bring Christ up from the dead).” But what does it say?"}, {"start_ms": 51922, "end_ms": 67022, "text": "“The word is near you; it is in your mouth and in your heart,” that is, the word of faith we are proclaiming: that if you confess with your mouth, “Jesus is Lord,” and believe in your heart that God raised Him from the dead, you will be saved."}, {"start_ms": 67542, "end_ms": 73123, "text": "For with your heart you believe and are justified, and with your mouth you confess and are saved."}, {"start_ms": 74023, "end_ms": 89083, "text": "It is just as the Scripture says: “Anyone who believes in Him will never be put to shame.” For there is no difference between Jew and Greek: The same Lord is Lord of all, and gives richly to all who call on Him, for,"}, {"start_ms": 89603, "end_ms": 97424, "text": "“Everyone who calls on the name of the Lord will be saved.” How then can they call on the One in whom they have not believed?"}, {"start_ms": 97864, "end_ms": 101084, "text": "And how can they believe in the One of whom they have not heard?"}, {"start_ms": 101644, "end_ms": 104084, "text": "And how can they hear without someone to preach?"}, {"start_ms": 104844, "end_ms": 107184, "text": "And how can they preach unless they are sent?"}, {"start_ms": 107824, "end_ms": 115664, "text": "As it is written: “How beautiful are the feet of those who bring good news!” But not all of them welcomed the good news."}, {"start_ms": 116144, "end_ms": 124725, "text": "For Isaiah says, “Lord, who has believed our message?” Consequently, faith comes by hearing, and hearing by the word of Christ."}, {"start_ms": 125305, "end_ms": 127425, "text": "But I ask, did they not hear?"}, {"start_ms": 127925, "end_ms": 137885, "text": "Indeed they did: “Their voice has gone out into all the earth, their words to the ends of the world.” I ask instead, did Israel not understand?"}, {"start_ms": 138585, "end_ms": 152026, "text": "First, Moses says: “I will make you jealous by those who are not a nation; I will make you angry by a nation without understanding.” And Isaiah boldly says: “I was found by those who did not seek Me;"}, {"start_ms": 152506, "end_ms": 163346, "text": "I revealed Myself to those who did not ask for Me.” But as for Israel he says: “All day long I have held out My hands to a disobedient and obstinate people.”"}], "words": [{"t": "Romans,", "s": 2080, "e": 2540, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 2740, "e": 3080, "si": 0}, {"t": "Ten.", "s": 3140, "e": 3380, "si": 0}, {"t": "Brothers,", "s": 4840, "e": 5300, "si": 1}, {"t": "my", "s": 5580, "e": 5700, "si": 1}, {"t": "heart’s", "s": 5800, "e": 6160, "si": 1}, {"t": "desire", "s": 6240, "e": 6740, "si": 1}, {"t": "and", "s": 6820, "e": 6960, "si": 1}, {"t": "prayer", "s": 7040, "e": 7300, "si": 1}, {"t": "to", "s": 7340, "e": 7420, "si": 1}, {"t": "God", "s": 7500, "e": 7740, "si": 1}, {"t": "for", 